<section id="the-idea">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading reveal">
            <span class="kicker">The big idea</span>
            <h2>Your project isn't one repo. It's a fleet of them.</h2>
            <p>Frontend, backend, a couple of microservices, and the infra-as-code repo everyone pretends doesn't exist. Fleet treats all of it as one project — because that's what it actually is.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rule-columns">
            <div class="rule-col reveal">
                <span class="rule-kicker">One orchestrator</span>
                <p>It holds the whole project in its head, so you don't have to hold five repos in yours.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-col reveal">
                <span class="rule-kicker">Minimal instructions</span>
                <p>Each repo's agent gets exactly the context it needs — not a novel, not your team's Slack history.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rule-col reveal">
                <span class="rule-kicker">Worktrees, not chaos</span>
                <p>Need two branches of the same repo running at once? Fleet spins up a worktree instead of making you pick.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
